**How to implement.** Stage 1 of a staged fit calibrates the instruments on the Calibration runs by the reference AIR calibration (001 §L 'stage 1 calibrates items on Calibration runs (the Eigenvalue Calibration Method)'; the S11.3 brief 'the Eigenvalue Calibration Method path over the AIR runs'): the study's AIR runs are handed, family by family, to S10.3's stage one (`calibrateFromAirRows`, step 388), and its constants become the instruments' parameter values. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `StudyEngine.fs`, after `fitNonlinear` (step 387): (1) `type Angle with member this.parameterValue : ParameterValue`, the angle in radians (`ParameterValue.angle`, step 246, is the reading the other way), and `type Retardance with member this.parameterValue : ParameterValue` (`MuellerReconstruction.fs:Retardance`), in radians. (2) `type StagedStudy with member this.calibrateLinear (context : StudyForwardContext) (prefits : ExperimentPrefit list) (solver : MuellerSolverProxy) : Result<StudyFitSolution, StudyFitError>`, taken only where `engineWith` (step 386) found the calibration shape: over the context with `kit.items` replaced by `this.items`, its layout (step 372) and each fitted run's family, its prep item's `calibrationPolarizerOpt` `familyWith` its analyzer item's (step 386); `StageOneAirRows` (step 388) of the capture rows (its prefit's `Ok (CapturePoints rows)`, exclusions applied by `keptBy`, step 314) of every Dark run among the prefits, in prefit order, and of the `LpLp`, `LpCpl` and `CplLp` runs, each in study order; then `StagedMuellerPath.calibrateFromAirRows solver` of them, an error answering the new `StagedPathFitErr of error : StagedMuellerError`, rendered `the staged Mueller path refused the fit: <the error's describe>` (step 388). Each layout entry takes its constant: an `LpLp` run's analyzer's `dialZero` the `lpZero`; an `LpCpl` run's analyzer's `dialZero` the `cplZero` and its `c2.retardance` the `cplAnalyzerRetardance`; a `CplLp` run's prep's `c2.fastAxisOffset` the source model's `thetaRel` less 45° (the built-in circular polarizer's retarder sits at 45° plus its offset, step 210) and its `c2.retardance` the source model's `retardance`, each through `parameterValue`. The answer is `{ engine = LinearStudyEngine; layout; members = [ { start = <the start vector's values>; outcome = MemberConverged (<those values>, None) } ]; fitted = <those values>; objectMatrices = [] }`: the cosine fits report no common chi-squared. The dark mean is the stage one's own, over every Dark run, as the reference reads it (step 349). No other mapping, constant or option is added. Tests, in `StudyEngineTests`, over a test-local truth `StageOneCalibrationData` (dark 5, `lpZero` 3°, `cplZero` −2°, `cplAnalyzerRetardance` 88°, source `thetaRel` 46° and `retardance` 91°), items made by `ItemDraft`: LP1 (`PolarizerPresetChoice` of the ideal LP, prep), LP2 (the real linear polarizer model, `DialMounted DialNegative`, its `dialZero` unknown, analyzer), CPL1 (the circular polarizer model, its `c2.fastAxisOffset` and `c2.retardance` unknown, prep), CPL2 (the circular polarizer model, `DialMounted DialPositive`, its `dialZero` and `c2.retardance` unknown, analyzer) and a Phone (the intensity detector model, `gain` known 1000); AIR setups LP1→LP2, LP1→CPL2 and CPL1→LP2 with empty object slots, a Calibration experiment over each scanning `VaryDialReading` 0° to 160° by 20°, and a Dark experiment, whose data a test-local `ExperimentDataProxy` answers as `CapturePoints` rows: each AIR row's `avgTotal` is 1000 · `airIdentityPred` of the truth's source model (`LpSource` behind LP1, `cplSource` behind CPL1) and its `lpAnalyzer` or `cplAnalyzer` (`analyzerBaseRow` at the dial) plus 5, each dark row 5: `the calibration stage recovers the instruments' zeros, retardances and offset through the reference stage one`: `calibrateLinear` with `createMathNetSvd ()` answers `LinearStudyEngine`, LP2's and CPL2's `dialZero` equal to 3° and −2° within 1e-9, and each of the five fitted values equal exactly to the constant `calibrateFromAirRows` answers over the same rows; `a calibration stage without a dark run is refused with the staged path's error`: without the Dark experiment it answers `StagedPathFitErr (EmptyCaptureSetErr _)` naming the darkness rows. `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After stage 1 lands, `StagedStudy.calibrateLinear` MUST hand the study's AIR runs by family and its Dark runs to `calibrateFromAirRows` and give each instrument entry its reference constant; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the calibration stage recovers the instruments' zeros, retardances and offset through the reference stage one` and `a calibration stage without a dark run is refused with the staged path's error`, the count rising by 2, and the widened `every study-fit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
